KNOWNBUG: N5008 [temp.param]/11 -- a function-template parameter pack may be
followed by further (deducible or defaulted) template parameters.  CBMC's
deduction mis-aligns the trailing parameter with its argument once the pack is
expanded, so `first(5,6,7)` for
`template<class U, class... W, class X = void> int first(U, W...)` is rejected
("found no match" / CONVERSION ERROR) even though it is well-formed.  This is the
current root cause of cpp17_tuple_basic (std::_Tuple_impl's forwarding
constructor has a template parameter after its pack).  Flip to CORE once a
template parameter following a parameter pack is deduced/instantiated correctly.
